# Dashboard Shell (`dashboard-shell`)

Collapsible spring sidebar with a gliding active indicator, period tabs, KPI tickers with sparklines and a self-drawing chart.

## What it should do
Build an analytics dashboard shell: a sidebar that springs between 208px and 64px (labels fade out, icons keep aria-labels, badge moves to the icon corner), a shared-layout active-item highlight, a header with 7d/30d/90d tabs, a 4-up KPI grid with tickers + sparklines, and a line chart that draws on view.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **motion**.
- Install dependencies: `npm i motion lucide-react`
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/dashboard-shell.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).
- Motion tokens go at `lib/kinetik/tokens.ts` (source below). Use tokens instead of magic numbers.

## Built from these kinetik components
Install them first (each also has its own prompt at `https://marvzkineticlibrary.vercel.app/r/<id>.prompt.md`):
```bash
npx shadcn@latest add https://marvzkineticlibrary.vercel.app/r/stat-counter-grid.json https://marvzkineticlibrary.vercel.app/r/chart-line-draw.json https://marvzkineticlibrary.vercel.app/r/animated-tabs.json
```

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** Collapsed icons keep aria-labels; aria-current on the active page; toggle button labelled.
- **Performance:** Sidebar width springs on one element; labels mount/unmount with short fades.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

